---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../../styles/directions/round.css";
---

<Base title="ARMS direction round — coded options" description="Three real running coded ARMS site directions." unindexed>
  <div class="round-shell">
    <section class="round-hero">
      <p class="round-kicker">ARMS site direction round · replacement</p>
      <h1>Three real running coded options.</h1>
      <p class="round-lead">
        These are not static previews. Each option is a clickable page with live layout, theme switching,
        real console proof, keyboard-reachable controls and reduced-motion fallbacks. The research base is
        Jay's scored taste corpus, not a fresh guess.
      </p>
      <div class="round-proof">
        <span>scored taste corpus</span>
        <span>real console proof</span>
        <span>light + dark</span>
        <span>desktop + 390px</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="round-grid" aria-label="Coded direction options">
      <a class="round-card signal" href="/look/directions/signal-objects/">
        <span class="round-index">A</span>
        <h2>Signal objects</h2>
        <p>Raw-and-bold discipline: strong type, mono truth, dense ordered rows, one accent, object-like panels.</p>
        <span class="round-open">Open the running option</span>
      </a>
      <a class="round-card clay" href="/look/directions/clay-observatory/">
        <span class="round-index">B</span>
        <h2>Clay observatory</h2>
        <p>Clean premium warmth: calm clay surfaces, generous breathing space, soft colour, crafted empty states.</p>
        <span class="round-open">Open the running option</span>
      </a>
      <a class="round-card spectrum" href="/look/directions/spectrum-console/">
        <span class="round-index">C</span>
        <h2>Spectrum console</h2>
        <p>Product as the page: dense console rows, semantic chart colours, neon-leaning but no glow.</p>
        <span class="round-open">Open the running option</span>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="round-notes">
      <h2>What changed after the rejected round</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The old round showed stills; this round is the coded thing itself.</li>
        <li>The directions start from Jay's scored references: raw-and-bold, cozy-and-calm, clean premium and the console ruler.</li>
        <li>Every option uses the same truthful ARMS copy and the public-safe real-console captures from the deployed build.</li>
        <li>Combinations are valid: a structure can be picked with another option's colour discipline.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
